// Tier W4: a fixed-width integer exposes the same closed method surface as `int` (the bit intrinsics
// and the `to_<type>` conversions), so an unknown method is rejected statically — with the real width
// in the message — rather than deferred to a runtime "no method" error. `to_u9` is not a valid width.
// expect: error E0007 at 6:6
// expect: exit 1
echo 200u8.to_u9()
